---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import {images} from '../data/images';
import {href} from '../data/site';

const testimonials = [
 {name:'Emma, USA',quote:[`In my mentoring experience I was able to have practice with regression, finding the inner child, finding a safe space, and exploring where and what she needed. I was able to practice this even more as I journaled. Journaling led me to other threads of healing when I realized I needed a compassionate soft father and I was able to be this for the inner child in my session.`,`Mentoring tied in everything I learned together and made it easier to model into my everyday life and even with helping others reflect and tap into that part of their inner child.`,`Amy's program works and has been a breath of fresh air. I've learned so much and Amy has helped me listen to my inner voice and intuitively find threads that needed to be discovered.`]},
 {name:'Amy, USA',quote:[`After completing the Inner Child workshop, my inner child felt safe, heard, seen, and secure. During the mentoring process, it allowed my Inner Child to grow more secure and gain additional understanding in order to trust my Caring Adult even more and with greater confidence.`,`Working with Amy, who I consider brilliant, is kind, compassionate, patient and truly a diamond in leading, guiding, and walking beside me throughout the process.`]},
 {name:'Rita, UK',quote:[`Amy is an experienced mentor and I drew valuable insights & lessons from her. Always compassionate, kind and a real sense of calm, which I feel is important on such a journey working with the inner child.`]},
 {name:'Ayelet, USA',quote:[`First of all my mentor Amy is INCREDIBLE! She is patient, calm, understanding and so very gentle. Her words touch my soul! She knows just what to say! She is flexible to help me with my individual needs. And she uses different techniques to help me get to a real true healing with my inner child.`]},
 {name:'Annie, Australia',quote:[`I can not say enough about Amy who was my mentor. She was supportive and guided me during this journey. Amy has a wealth of knowledge and she is always calm and approachable, which was so helpful when I was going through some major shifts in my life. I felt supported without judgement which is important to me. The mentoring program helped me have a deeper understanding of myself and a better connection with my Inner Child.`]},
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Inner Child Mentoring | Holistic Therapy | Amy Grist" description="Inner Child Mentoring with Amy is trauma-informed, heart-centered guidance to deepen integration, nurture healing and expand personal growth." ogImage={images[122]}>
 <PageHero image={images[122]} title="Inner Child Mentoring" caption="Ongoing Support for your journey" alt="Colourful layered portrait representing the inner child"/>
 <article class="mentoring-page">
  <section class="band opening"><div class="container">
   <blockquote><p>The mentoring program is the next level of growth and maturity with the Inner Child. It allows you and your inner child to continue to develop insight and awareness into how the wounds of childhood affect your adult life today.</p><cite>— Amy Y, USA</cite></blockquote>
  </div></section>
  <section class="band main-copy"><div class="container copy sections">
   <section><h2>Continuing the Journey of Integration</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>After completing the <a href="/inner-child-therapy/"><strong>Inner Child Workshop</strong></a>, the following weeks and months become a vital stage of your integration journey. This is where your relationship with your Inner Child deepens. It’s a time of digesting the material, reflecting on your experiences, and weaving the tools you’ve learned into your daily life.</p><p>Integration requires patience, gentleness and consistency. Mentoring offers a supportive, guided container to nurture this connection and help you navigate the shifts, openings and insights that continue to arise.</p></section>
   <section><h2>Who Inner Child Mentoring Is For</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>Inner Child Mentoring is ideal for anyone who has completed the Inner Child Workshop and feels ready to deepen the journey. It may resonate with you if:</p><ul><li>you want continued support while integrating the workshop</li><li>you feel emotional or energetic shifts and want guidance processing them</li><li>old patterns or memories are resurfacing and you’d like clarity on their meaning</li><li>you’re seeking accountability and a safe space to stay connected to the work</li><li>you want to strengthen trust, dialogue and playfulness with your Inner Child</li><li>you sense deeper layers of healing ready to unfold</li><li>you desire companionship, grounding and reassurance along your path</li><li>you value a long-term relationship with your inner world, nurtured with care</li></ul><p>Mentoring meets you exactly where you are, honouring your rhythm, your readiness, and your inner landscape.</p></section>
   <section><h2>What to Expect in Mentoring Sessions</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>Mentoring sessions are gentle, trauma-informed, and tailored to your personal journey. Sessions can be weekly or every two weeks, depending on what best supports your integration.</p><p>Together, we explore:</p><ul><li>insights, memories or emotions arising from your Inner Child practice</li><li>limiting beliefs and subconscious patterns ready to be rewired</li><li>hidden, forgotten or suppressed aspects of the child self</li><li>past wounds, trauma imprints, attachment patterns or emotional blocks</li><li>relationship dynamics connected to childhood conditioning</li><li>nervous system responses, resistance and protective parts</li><li>your ongoing connection and communication with your Inner Child</li></ul><p>Between sessions, if something meaningful arises, you’re invited to share it. Support and guidance are available throughout the process as part of holding the integrity of your inner work.</p></section>
  </div></section>
  <section class="band rose"><div class="container copy rose-sections">
   <section><h2>Benefits of Inner Child Mentoring</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>As you continue nurturing the relationship with your Inner Child, you may experience:</p><ul><li>deeper emotional clarity and self-awareness</li><li>a calmer, more regulated nervous system</li><li>softened anxiety, fear or self-doubt</li><li>renewed intuition, creativity and inner wisdom</li><li>healthier communication and boundaries</li><li>integration of old memories and emotional patterns</li><li>increased self-compassion and inner safety</li><li>conscious, balanced relationship dynamics</li><li>greater confidence to express your authentic self</li><li>a sense of inner harmony, belonging and wholeness</li></ul><p>Mentoring supports these shifts to unfold gently and sustainably, honouring your pace and celebrating your growth.</p></section>
   <section><h2>Deepening the Practice</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>Mentoring offers the opportunity to revisit and deepen the Inner Child meditation techniques learned in the workshop. Together, we may explore:</p><ul><li>guided regressions</li><li>imaginal dialogues</li><li>somatic awareness practices</li><li>emotional release techniques</li><li>ancestral and generational healing threads</li></ul><p>Letting go of long-held beliefs, emotions and protective strategies requires tenderness. Mentoring creates the safety needed to peel back layers of conditioning and automatic responses, allowing healing to unfold naturally.</p><p>Resistance, doubt and fear are all normal parts of the journey. With support, these moments become opportunities for profound insight, self-trust and emotional integration. All parts of your <em>inner community</em> are welcomed and honoured here.</p></section>
  </div></section>
  <section class="band closing-copy"><div class="container copy sections">
   <section><h2>A Journey of Ongoing Growth</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>Integration typically unfolds over <strong>three to six months</strong>, though many choose to continue longer-term mentoring — from <strong>12 months to two years</strong> — to support deeper transformation and continued alignment.</p><p>Whether short-term or long-term, mentoring provides dedicated space to stay connected to your practice, explore emerging insights, and anchor new ways of being.</p></section>
   <section><h2>Your Introductory Mentoring Call</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>In your <strong>free introductory call</strong>, we open a safe space for gentle enquiry. Here we identify patterns, blocks or challenges arising in your daily life and explore what your Inner Child is currently communicating.</p><p>By the end of the call, you will have:</p><ul><li>clarity on the imbalances or wounds asking for attention</li><li>insight into what stage of integration you’re in</li><li>guidance on the next steps in your healing journey</li></ul></section>
   <section><h2>Working Together</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>Each session is guided at your pace and tailored to your individual needs. I hold space with care, respect, confidentiality and attunement, allowing what arises to unfold naturally.</p><p>Every session includes quiet time to ground, reflect and integrate, ensuring that what you receive is held with clarity and compassion.</p></section>
  </div></section>
  <section class="band enquiry center" id="iccontact"><div class="container"><h2>Ready to Continue Your Inner Child Journey?</h2><hr class="rule short"/><p>If you feel called to deepen your connection with your Inner Child, I warmly invite you to reach out.<br/>Together, we’ll nurture your inner world, honour your pace, and expand your capacity for joy, safety, confidence and authentic expression.</p><h3>Enquire about Inner Child Mentoring</h3><hr class="rule short"/><a class="button" href={href('/contact/')}>Get in touch</a></div></section>
  <section class="band soft-rose experiences"><div class="container center"><h2>Here’s what people are saying about their Mentoring experiences:</h2><hr class="rule short"/><div class="testimonial-grid">{testimonials.map(item => <figure><blockquote>{item.quote.map(paragraph => <p>“{paragraph}”</p>)}</blockquote><figcaption>{item.name}</figcaption></figure>)}</div></div></section>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.opening{padding-bottom:20px}.opening blockquote{max-width:930px;margin:auto;text-align:center;font:400 25px/1.5 var(--heading);color:var(--ink)}.opening cite{font:300 14px var(--body);font-style:normal}.main-copy{padding-top:25px}.sections,.rose-sections{display:grid;gap:46px}.sections h2,.rose-sections h2{font-size:32px;margin:0}.sections .rule,.rose-sections .rule{margin:14px 0 24px}.sections a{}.rose-sections{gap:42px}.closing-copy{padding-bottom:45px}.enquiry{background:#f1dddd}.enquiry .rule{margin-inline:auto}.enquiry p{max-width:900px;margin-inline:auto;margin-bottom:28px}.enquiry h3{font-size:28px;margin-top:35px}.form-note{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink);margin-top:18px!important}.experiences{color:var(--ink)}.experiences h2{font-size:32px}.experiences .rule{margin-inline:auto}.testimonial-grid{display:grid;gap:25px;margin-top:35px;text-align:left}.testimonial-grid figure{margin:0;background:#f5f5f5;padding:32px 38px}.testimonial-grid blockquote p{text-align:left;margin-bottom:16px}.testimonial-grid figcaption{text-align:right;font:400 18px var(--heading);color:var(--menu-heading)}
@media(max-width:799px){.opening blockquote{font-size:22px}.sections h2,.rose-sections h2,.experiences h2{font-size:28px}.copy p{text-align:left}.testimonial-grid figure{padding:27px 25px}}
</style>
